## Pin fixture — mixin default method body with `self.<required>`
## reference and `String` interpolation.
##
## Exercises the spec/types/mixin_default_methods.spec.md B2 shape:
##  * `Greeter` declares `def name -> String` (required, no body) and
##    `def greet -> String` (default body) that interpolates
##    `self.name`.
##  * `Bot` implements `name` and inherits `greet` via `include
##    Greeter`.
##
## Regression guard for the bootstrap-class-stomp issue
## (project_ruxen_resolve_class_stomps_typealias): before option (a)
## landed in resolve_type_expr, the interpolation result (Ty::String)
## could not unify with the declared return type
## (Ty::Class { name: "String" }), surfacing as
## `expected `String`, found `String`` from typeck/unify.rs.
mixin Greeter
  def name -> String
  def greet -> String
    "Hello, #{self.name}!"
  end
end

class Bot
  nm: String

  def init(@nm: String)
  end

  include Greeter

  def name -> String
    self.nm.clone
  end
end

def main
  let b = Bot.new("Riv")
  puts "#{b.greet}"
end
